    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\n\nIn Python 3.15, [PEP 782]( https://peps.python.org/pep-0782/ ) was accepted and implemented, which provides the `PyBytesWriter` API. This supersedes previous approaches like constructing a `bytes` object to fill with [`PyBytes_FromStringAndSize(NULL, s)`]( https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/bytes.html#c.PyBytes_FromStringAndSize ). The [Python docs include this example]( https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/bytes.html#update-pybytes-fromstringandsize-code ):\n\n> **Update ``PyBytes_FromStringAndSize()`` code**\n> \n> Example of code using the soft deprecated ``PyBytes_FromStringAndSize(NULL, size)`` API:\n> \n> ```c\n> int copy_bytes(char *dest, const char *src, Py_ssize_t num_bytes)\n> {\n>     ...\n> }\n> \n> PyObject* create_string(const char *start, Py_ssize_t num_bytes)\n> {\n>     PyObject *result = PyBytes_FromStringAndSize(NULL, num_bytes);\n>     if (result == NULL) {\n>         return NULL;\n>     }\n>     if (copy_bytes(PyBytes_AS_STRING(result), start, num_bytes) < 0) {\n>         Py_CLEAR(result);\n>     }\n>     return result;\n> }\n> ```\n> \n> It can now be updated to:\n> \n> ```c\n> PyObject* create_string(const char *start, Py_ssize_t num_bytes)\n> {\n>     PyBytesWriter *writer = PyBytesWriter_Create(num_bytes);\n>     if (writer == NULL) {\n>         return NULL;\n>     }\n>     if (copy_bytes(PyBytesWriter_GetData(writer), start, num_bytes) < 0) {\n>         PyBytesWriter_Discard(writer);\n>         return NULL;\n>     }\n>     return PyBytesWriter_Finish(writer);\n> }\n> ```\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like.\n\nTwo things that would be good to adapt to this change:\n\n1. Extending [`cpython/bytes.pxd`]( https://github.com/cython/cython/blob/1f7e6ddaf16c7087a366dc9a9508b09c682fa0a3/Cython/Includes/cpython/bytes.pxd ) to include the new APIs\n2. Changing internal code to use the Python 3.15 path when appropriate (new enough version & currently not stable ABI IIUC). Need to benchmark changes to confirm there is not a slowdown.\n\n### Describe alternatives you've considered.\n\nOpen to other approaches to integration.\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
